{"severity":"error","file":"errors/cap_widen_4.march","start_line":6,"start_col":4,"end_line":6,"end_col":17,"message":"`Cap(IO.Console)` cannot be widened to `Cap(IO.FileWrite)` — `cap_narrow` only attenuates, so the source capability must subsume the target.\nhelp: `Cap(IO.FileWrite)` is not below `Cap(IO.Console)` in the capability lattice. Receive it from a caller that holds an ancestor of it.","code":"cap_widen","fix":null,"labels":[],"notes":[]}
{"severity":"error","file":"errors/cap_widen_4.march","start_line":9,"start_col":2,"end_line":12,"end_col":5,"message":"`main` is granted `Cap(IO.Console)`, but the program reaches `IO.FileWrite` (reached from `main`: main → as_writer). The grant is a ceiling on the WHOLE program — declaring `needs IO.FileWrite` does not raise it.\nhelp: add a `Cap(IO.FileWrite)` parameter to `main` (e.g. `fn main(…, _cap_filewrite : Cap(IO.FileWrite))`), or widen the whole grant to `Cap(IO)`, or remove the use.","code":"cap_grant_exceeded","fix":null,"labels":[],"notes":[]}
